From cefebea4690df5083876169c2be64fbe03f2aeea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The browser Authors <noreply@browser.invalid>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 17:13:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 31/55] stable-version

The full version in the user agent's client hints is the Chrome release
of this major version that the stable channel serves now, not the one the
build was cut from. The list of served releases
(versionhistory.googleapis.com) is fetched at most once a day and kept
beside the default user data directory; each profile draws one by rollout
share, never older than the one it reported before, applied through
--fingerprint-brand-version-long. Never another major version; not with
--use-chromium-defaults or an explicit brand version. The request goes
through the system network context, so a --proxy-server on the command
line carries it; it is made whatever --disable-background-networking says,
and only --use-chromium-defaults or an explicit brand version turns it off.
